<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>5.15.6: Lesson Summary</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01525</md:content-id>
    <md:title>5.15.6: Lesson Summary</md:title>
    <md:uuid>16c2e7c2-7a7c-4367-a841-c47ee37b623e</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>In this lesson, you learned how to:</para>
<list>
  <item> Calculate rates of change of functions given graphs, equations, or tables.</item>
  <item> Use rates of change to describe how a linear function and an exponential function change over equal intervals.</item>
</list>
<para>Here are the<emphasis> activities</emphasis> that helped you reach those goals:</para>
<list>
  <item> 5.15.1: Writing Equivalent Expressions</item>
  <list>
    <item> In this activity, you practiced writing equivalent expressions using the order of operations, combining like terms, and using properties of exponents.</item>
  </list>
  <item> 5.15.2: Linear Function Constant Rate of Change</item>
  <list>
    <item> In this activity, you revisited and extended your understanding of the constant rate of change for a linear function.</item>
    <item> 5.15.2: Self Check </item>
    <item> 5.15.2: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 5.15.3: Growth Rate of an Exponential Function</item>
  <list>
    <item> In this activity, you examined what happens to the values of an exponential function \(f\) when the input is increased by 1 and then when its value changes by a factor of \(b\).</item>
    <item> 5.15.3: Self Check </item>
    <item> 5.15.3: Additional Resources </item>
  </list>
  <item> 5.15.4: Comparing Linear and Exponential Growth</item>
  <list>
    <item> In this activity, you compared linear and exponential growth.</item>
  </list>
</list>
<para>After these activities, you completed the following <emphasis>practice</emphasis>:</para>
<list>
  <item> 5.15.5: Practice</item>
</list>
<section class="check-understanding"><title>Checking In</title><exercise id="_68c90734-a21b-4539-badf-867b0ee4808e" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>On a scale of 1 to 5, how confident do you feel about the learning goals of this lesson?</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Nice reflection! You learn more when you take the time to reflect on your thinking.</para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
